notes:
MECHANICAL SWEEP RESULT: grep -c '<table' returns 0 for EVERY file in this page's candidate set (28 files swept, including all 19 must-reads and all 15 ALSO RELEVANT files). There is no raw-HTML table anywhere in the Company Locations documentation, so fromRawHtmlTable is false on every record here and that is a verified count, not a default. The one raw-<table> file the recon flagged, sample-record-type-210-91f4d609.md, is a HISTORICAL-INVOICE sample record (210,true), not the PO Bill-To 210 address record, and was correctly ruled out.

CENSUS DEFECT CONFIRMED AND WORKED AROUND: add-a-shipping-or-billing-address-3b51c816.md scores grep -c '^|' = 0 but grep -cE '^ *\|' = 40, because SAP indents the table four spaces inside a numbered step. Any pipe-table census anchored at start-of-line would have missed this page's ONLY field catalog. The indented anchor was used for the whole sweep.

TABLES FOUND AND FULLY ENUMERATED (5 settings/catalog tables, 0 sampled, 0 truncated):
  (1) the 12-row Company Locations address field table (add-a-shipping-or-billing-address-3b51c816.md) — all 12 rows emitted;
  (2) the 11-row PO Bill-to 210 import column table — all 11 rows emitted;
  (3) the 11-row PO Ship-to 220 import column table — all 11 rows emitted;
  (4) the 249-row Country Code List — all 249 rows emitted as one unwired value set;
  (5) the 4-row Peppol Limitations table — its Company Locations row is emitted as a dependency, not a field, because it describes a matching rule rather than a control.

ILLUSTRATIVE / OUT-OF-SCOPE TABLES DELIBERATELY SKIPPED, and why: the 23-row Revision History table in company-locations-8b49554d.md is a dating artefact, not a settings table — skipped as a catalog but mined for dating evidence and quoted in field notes (April 14, 2018 email address field; September 9, 2016 VAT ID and optional State/Province; March 18, 2016 State/Province became a list; September 17, 2014 'two user interfaces'). The revision-history table in country-code-list-8b3e41a4.md is likewise dating-only and contains NO codes. The field table in step-4-add-a-new-tax-authority-7f90cede.md (Tax Authority Name / Country / State/Province / Tax Name ...) is the Tax Authorities wizard's own settings table and belongs to a Tax Administration page, not here — skipped under the page-ownership rule and emitted only as a dependency. The four 'The Import Template: Fields and Descriptions' tables (8b51ca3d, 8b52534d, 8b53850b, 8b640ac7) were each opened and checked: all four are VENDOR-side templates (Vendor Code / Address Code / Level 1-10 Code, vendor banking, vendor master) and none is the Company Locations import template.

PUBLISHABLE DOCUMENTED GAP: the Company Locations IMPORT TEMPLATE COLUMN LIST DOES NOT EXIST IN THIS CORPUS. import-shipping-or-billing-addresses-601c2549.md offers only 'Select Download the import template link if you want to download a template with the field names already filled in' — the field names themselves are never printed. I searched both guide directories for every 'import template' topic and for every file containing 'Address Code' or 'ship-to address'; the nearest documented column sets are the PO 210/220 records, which are a DIFFERENT import with a different required-field profile (State/Province Y there, Optional on the page). A config writer automating the Company Locations import has no documented column order to work from. Thin is the correct answer here and no columns were invented.

WHAT I COULD NOT DETERMINE: (a) the accepted value list for the page's Country Code field — no list is documented and the only 249-row catalog is scoped to the vendor import, so it is recorded unwired; (b) the State/Province list contents — the revision history says it became a list in March 2016 but the entries are never enumerated, so fieldType is 'unknown' rather than 'dropdown'; (c) whether Country Code is a text box or a list; (d) any character limits on the page's own fields (only the import records carry limits); (e) the default state of the 'Add address as a Ship To Location as well' check box; (f) which European countries make VAT ID required; (g) the columns of the Company Locations grid itself; (h) the contents of the Import Summary page and the 'Ship To Locations import history' section. No No/Yes pairs were completed and no values were inferred.

SCOPE DECISIONS: prose-only controls of this page (the New, Modify, Remove, Import, Export All and Save buttons, the 'Download the import template' link, the Browse/Open sequence, the 'Remove selected Company Locations' confirmation, the Add New Ship To Location / Modify Ship To Location / Import Ship To Locations windows, and the Ship To Address / Bill To Address type-ahead search field) appear in no table and are left to the procedural lens — they were read and are described in contradictions and field notes where they bear on a table row. The Ship To / Bill To tab IS emitted as a field because it is the context that makes the two tabs' field sets non-identical (VAT ID is bill-to only). The 22 PO import columns are emitted with a loud NOT-A-PAGE-CONTROL prefix in every note so they can be re-homed if a Purchase Order Import node is built; they are kept because they are two complete column catalogs that exist nowhere else in the graph and because the corpus explicitly binds them to this page through Address Code = External ID.

ROLE NOTE (not a contradiction): the Invoice Configuration (Restricted) administrator role can use Company Locations, per required-roles-476a5f62.md, which differs from that role's exclusion from the Group Configurations tool — per-page visibility, not a conflicting rule.
